# .cursorrules — for Cursor IDE

## Endpoint
```
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://allrouter.ai/v1
OPENAI_API_KEY=<your-allrouter-key>
```

## Models available in Cursor via AllRouter
- `Kimi-K3` — default for agentic coding (best price/perf)
- `claude-sonnet-4-6` — when you need maximum accuracy
- `gpt-5.5-openai-compact` — when you need OpenAI-ecosystem tools
- `GLM5.2` — free tier for explain / docs / tests
- `gemma-4-31b-it` — ultra cheap bulk analysis ($0.10/M)

## Cursor Model Settings
Add to Cursor's "OpenAI Compatible" model list:
- Name: `Kimi-K3 (AllRouter)`
- Base URL: `https://allrouter.ai/v1`
- API Key: `sk-allrouter-...`

## System prompt snippets worth keeping
1. Always prefer `Kimi-K3` for multi-file refactors — it's 12× cheaper than Claude with only 6pp pass-rate delta.
2. Use `GLM5.2` for documentation/explanation tasks — it's nearly free.
3. Always check `x-allrouter-upstream-model` on responses when debugging — verifies you're getting the real model.
